{u}=\\langle 3,-2 \\rangle$ and $\\textbf{v}=\\langle 6, -4 \\rangle.$" 13194139534901 true] [17592186100614 1145 "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/assets/b25d71fb75afcb5e4f9e8ce137ec69fb1dfda54aa544b1636e11503273527844.png)\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-4)-6\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $\\det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA = |\\,0\\,| = 0\n$$" 13194139534901 true] [17592186100614 1145 "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(M) &= \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot (-4) - 6 \\cdot (-2) \\\\\n&= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $\\det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA = \\mid \\,0\\, \\mid = 0\n$$" 13194139534901 false] [17592186100791 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318430 13194139534901 true] [17592186100792 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318438 13194139534901 true] [17592186100792 1020 #edb/ref 17592186318442 13194139534901 true] [17592186268921 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043024/assets/7a70285258e584708a7296a2a008536dec9c97750b48e5fe0eb2f8cb7761bed1.png)\n\nCalculate the area of the parallelogram in the figure." 13194139534901 true] [17592186268921 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956518/assets/7a70285258e584708a7296a2a008536dec9c97750b48e5fe0eb2f8cb7761bed1.png)\n\nCalculate the area of the parallelogram in the figure." 13194139534901 false] [17592186268936 1000 